										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Morpheus8 is one of the few non-surgical treatments that tightens loose abdominal skin and remodels stubborn fat in a single session — delivering bipolar radiofrequency energy through insulated microneedles to depths that surface-level treatments cannot reach. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">At Med Aesthetics Miami, Rosanna Bermejo, MSN, Nurse Practitioner, Founder and President, builds every Morpheus8 treatment plan around your anatomy, your goals, and your safety. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">For post-pregnancy skin laxity, post-weight-loss contour concerns, or stubborn abdominal fat that resists diet and exercise, Morpheus8 offers a practitioner-led path to natural-looking results — without incisions, scarring, or surgical recovery.</span></p>
<h2><b>Key Takeaways</b></h2>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Morpheus8 is FDA-cleared and classified as a Subdermal Adipose Remodeling Device — it works at 2mm depth for skin tightening and 4mm depth for adipocyte remodeling in a single abdominal session.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Optimal results develop gradually over three to six months as the body&#8217;s collagen-induction response matures — visible improvement begins around weeks three to four.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">A full series of 3 treatments is recommended, spaced four to six weeks apart — body sessions are priced at $1,100 per session or $2,800 for the package of three at Med Aesthetics Miami.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Morpheus8 is safe for all Fitzpatrick skin types 1 through 6, making it appropriate for Miami&#8217;s ethnically diverse patient population.</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Loose abdominal skin and stubborn fat pockets do not respond to effort alone.</span><a href="https://www.medaestheticsmiami.com/appointments/"> <span style="font-weight: 400;">Book a Morpheus8 consultation</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;"> at Med Aesthetics Miami — Coral Gables, Aventura, or Lauderdale-By-The-Sea.</span></p>
<h2><b>What Is Morpheus8 and How Does It Work Beneath the Skin?</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Morpheus8 is a fractional device that pairs microneedling with targeted bipolar radiofrequency energy — available at Med Aesthetics Miami through the</span><a href="https://www.medaestheticsmiami.com/advanced-skin-treatments/morpheus8-miami/"> <span style="font-weight: 400;">Morpheus8 treatment program</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;"> — to remodel tissue at a subdermal level. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">The microneedles create controlled micro-injuries in the skin, triggering the body&#8217;s wound-healing cascade and stimulating the production of new collagen and elastin. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Radiofrequency energy travels through those needles to deliver precise heat below the surface, remodeling tissue where topical treatments and surface-level devices cannot reach.</span></p>
<h2><b>What makes Morpheus8 a Subdermal Adipose Remodeling Device</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Morpheus8&#8217;s classification as a Subdermal Adipose Remodeling Device (SARD) distinguishes it from surface-level skin treatments. The device delivers depth-adjustable treatment from 0.5mm to 8mm — and for the abdomen, Med Aesthetics Miami uses a two-depth protocol: 2mm to tighten the dermis and stimulate collagen, and 4mm to target adipocytes, the fat cells responsible for stubborn abdominal bulging. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">This dual-depth approach means one treatment addresses both skin laxity and the underlying fat layer simultaneously. The technology is FDA-cleared and safe for all Fitzpatrick skin types 1 through 6 — a meaningful distinction in a city as ethnically diverse as Miami.</span></p>
<h3><b>How radiofrequency energy triggers cellular rejuvenation</b></h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Radiofrequency heat reaching the subdermal tissue initiates a gradual cellular healing cascade — stimulating neocollagenesis, the formation of new collagen fibers, and elastinogenesis, the restoration of skin elasticity. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Research published in the</span><a href="https://jddonline.com/"> <span style="font-weight: 400;">Journal of Drugs in Dermatology</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;"> on fractional RF microneedling has documented measurable improvements in skin laxity, texture, and subdermal fat volume through sustained biological remodeling. The response unfolds over months, which is why Morpheus8 before-and-after results reflect a natural progression rather than an overnight change.</span></p>
<h3><b>Morpheus8 Stomach Treatment Parameters at a Glance </b></h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Morpheus8 for the abdomen uses a dual-depth protocol — 2mm to tighten skin and 4mm to remodel fat — within a single session, with results building over a recommended three-session series. The table below summarizes the core treatment parameters at Med Aesthetics Miami. </span></p>
