<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Results develop over 3 months post-treatment and hold for 12–18 months, based on outcomes reported in the RF microneedling clinical literature, before a maintenance session becomes relevant.</span></p>
<h2>What Affects Your Total Morpheus8 Investment?</h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Mild laxity resolves in 1 session at $1,000. Moderate laxity requires 2–3 sessions — $2,000 individually or $2,500 packaged. Significant laxity may warrant the full 3-session protocol plus an annual maintenance session at the single-session rate.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Clients adding eye-area treatment to a face-and-neck session pay $470 per eye session, or $1,155 for 3. Combining zones in the same appointment is possible — your technician will confirm sequencing and depth settings for each area at your</span><a href="https://www.medaestheticsmiami.com/appointments/"> <span style="font-weight: 400;">Morpheus8 consultation</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;">. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">For clients comparing all available RF microneedling options at the center, the</span><a href="https://www.medaestheticsmiami.com/morpheus8-comparison/"> <span style="font-weight: 400;">Morpheus8 comparison guide</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;"> explains how the treatment stacks up against alternatives in terms of device type, depth, and cost. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Most clients schedule one annual maintenance session at the $1,000 single-session rate to preserve the collagen remodeling achieved in the initial protocol.</span></p>
<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<p><b>How Much Does Morpheus8 Face and Neck Cost at Med Aesthetics Miami?</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Med Aesthetics Miami charges $1,000 per face-and-neck session. A package of 3 sessions costs $2,500, reducing the effective per-session rate to $833 and saving $500 versus paying individually. The neck-only protocol is available separately at $680 per session.</span></p>
<p><b>Why Does Morpheus8 Cost More at Some Miami Providers Than Others?</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Pricing reflects provider credentials, device designation, and session inclusions. InMode Top Provider clinics like Med Aesthetics Miami price mid-to-upper range because certified technicians, board-certified clinical oversight, and current device configurations add demonstrable value over discount-volume providers.</span></p>
<p><b>Does Med Aesthetics Miami Charge a Consultation Fee?</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">No separate consultation fee applies when booking a treatment session directly. Clients wanting a standalone skin assessment before committing to a protocol can book a wellness consultation separately to discuss goals, session count, and pricing before any treatment begins.</span></p>
<p><b>How Many Morpheus8 Sessions Does a Face and Neck Treatment Require?</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Mild laxity typically resolves in 1 session. Moderate laxity requires 2–3 sessions spaced 4–6 weeks apart. The certified team at Med Aesthetics Miami recommends a session count at consultation based on your skin condition — not a standard protocol applied to every patient.</span></p>
<p><b>Is Morpheus8 Face and Neck Covered by Insurance?</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">No. Morpheus8 is a cosmetic procedure and is not covered by health insurance in Florida. The full cost — $1,000 per session or $2,500 for 3 — is paid out of pocket. Some providers accept third-party financing plans; confirm availability at your consultation.</span></p>
<p><b>How Long Do Morpheus8 Face and Neck Results Last?</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Collagen remodeling from a completed Morpheus8 protocol typically lasts 12–18 months, based on outcomes reported in the RF microneedling clinical literature. Most clients schedule one annual maintenance session at the $1,000 single-session rate to preserve the structural improvement from the original course.</span></p>
<p><b>Can I Combine Face and Neck With Eye Treatment in the Same Visit?</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Yes. Med Aesthetics Miami offers Morpheus8 for the eye area for $470 per session. Combining zones in the same appointment is possible — your technician will advise on sequencing and depth settings for each area at consultation.</span></p>
<p><b>What Is the Difference Between a Face-Only and Face-and-Neck Session?</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">A face-and-neck session treats jawline laxity, jowls, cheeks, and forehead, as well as the neck, in a single appointment. Med Aesthetics Miami prices the combined session at $1,000 — making it a stronger value than paying face-only rates at providers who charge separately for each zone.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Loose skin along the jaw or neck responds to RF microneedling when delivered by a certified Top Provider team.</span><a href="https://www.medaestheticsmiami.com/appointments/"> <span style="font-weight: 400;">Reserve your face and neck session</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;"> at Med Aesthetics Miami and see results build over the following 3 months.</span></p>
